One of the most abundant minerals in the Earth’s crust, quartz is essential for manufacturing core components of smartphones and computers. Most of the world’s supply comes from a single mining district in the Appalachian Mountains of the southeast United States, which has become an unlikely linchpin of the global tech economy.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5168e916-7c72-11f1-9145-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Spruce-Pine-Pegmatite.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5168e916-7c72-11f1-9145-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Spruce-Pine-Pegmatite.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">984c269a-81c7-11f1-95a5-1f0843f75d2d</guid><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 16:02:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5168e916-7c72-11f1-9145-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Spruce-Pine-Pegmatite.png">© Marguliesgm, CC BY-SA 4.0 via Wikimedia Commons</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>US-Iran fighting escalates with infrastructure targeted</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260718-us-iran-fighting-escalates-with-infrastructure-targeted</link><description>
Iran on Saturday struck infrastructure in the Gulf and threatened a "full-scale offensive" in retaliation for the seventh consecutive night of US strikes on the Islamic republic.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3f5fe1d8-8227-11f1-96d1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/64be5ebe968fbf6d8c93cbaf54b722cd4931a830.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3f5fe1d8-8227-11f1-96d1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/64be5ebe968fbf6d8c93cbaf54b722cd4931a830.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e8ca91d0-82a1-11f1-b21d-b7dd12542a41</guid><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 12:12:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3f5fe1d8-8227-11f1-96d1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/64be5ebe968fbf6d8c93cbaf54b722cd4931a830.jpg">© - / US MARINE CORPS/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Syria taken off US terror blacklist after 47 years, paving way for investment</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260718-syria-taken-off-us-terror-blacklist-after-almost-47-years-paving-way-for-investment</link><description>
